{"repositoryId":1098539566,"availability":"available","full":"GeoffreyWang1117/Rate-Limiter-Service","name":"Rate-Limiter-Service","description":"Token-aware admission control for LLM inference: reserve/commit/expire budgeting on Redis + Lua, with lease reclamation, SLO-aware shedding, and measured results","category":"Finance","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2025-11-17T20:31:21Z","updated":"2026-10-15T10:16:07Z","branch":"feat/llm-admission-control","homepage":"https://geoffreywang1117.github.io/Rate-Limiter-Service/","topics":["admission-control","backpressure","distributed-systems","inference","llm","lua","rate-limiting","redis","slo","typescript"],"demo":"https://geoffreywang1117.github.io/Rate-Limiter-Service/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:44.249Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:44.249Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-15T11:20:44.249Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-15T11:20:44.249Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Token-aware admission control for LLM inference, on Redis and PostgreSQL.","A conventional API rate limiter charges every request one unit and decides once, at arrival. Neither half of that holds for inference traffic, so this service implements a three-phase protocol instead — reserve, commit, expire — and measures what that protocol costs.","Interactive demo → Drive the protocol in a browser: send requests, complete them, or abandon one and watch the hold sit there until the lease expires and the next admission reclaims it. The page reimplements the admission logic from src/llm/admission-scripts.ts and says so — it is not the service, and nothing on it is a latency measurement. The measured numbers on that page come from the artifacts in bench/results/."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/GeoffreyWang1117/Rate-Limiter-Service/blob/feat%2Fllm-admission-control/README.md","fingerprint":"809c60948d3f7382f88dc3c8507c7d03250